From 79c050659e861293b6b5950baaffd401cdf66d4e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 09:00:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 31/38] UML-DARWIN-LOCAL: um: return free guest pages to the
 Darwin host

mem= is a ceiling, not a reservation. setup_physmem() backs physical memory
with a sparse unlinked temp file mapped MAP_SHARED, so host pages appear on
first touch and a guest configured for more than it uses costs only what it
touched. Nothing ever gave those pages back, though, so a guest that peaked
once stayed expensive for the rest of its life. That is the wrong shape for a
phone, where the host may have 2 GiB in total and raising mem= is not an
option.

Register a free-page reporting driver. The buddy allocator already knows which
pages are free; punch the reported range out of the backing file with
F_PUNCHHOLE and the resident host pages are dropped at once. A measured probe
on APFS took a fully touched 1 GiB MAP_SHARED mapping from 1025 MiB resident
to 513 MiB by punching half of it, with the punched range reading back as zero
and re-materializing on the next write - so a reported page needs no fault-in
handshake before the guest can use it again.

phys_mapping() already returns the file offset for a physical address, and for
the physical-memory file that offset is the physical address itself, so the
driver needs no new address arithmetic. It only punches ranges that belong to
that file, leaving iomem regions alone.

The minimum order is 5 rather than the pageblock_order default. A 16 KiB
profile makes a pageblock 32 MiB and a busy guest rarely has a whole one free,
while 512 KiB still amortizes one host call across 32 pages.
page_reporting.page_reporting_order= overrides it.

A host that refuses to release the range disables reporting once instead of
failing a cycle every two seconds for the rest of the boot: losing the
optimization must not cost the guest anything else.

Change-Id: Ib1467f28b83163f678ccf6c68ffb20ac91457e62
---
 arch/um/include/shared/os.h |  3 ++
 arch/um/kernel/physmem.c    | 91 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 arch/um/os-Darwin/mem.c     | 30 ++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 124 insertions(+)

